title: 'SCOPE: the Swarm family is entirely absent - decide in or out'
updated: 2026-08-27T06:35:32Z
---

A scope question, not a defect. Six resource groups exist in the Engine API
and none is exposed:

  /swarm     init, join, leave, update, unlockkey, unlock
  /nodes     list, inspect, update, delete
  /services  list, create, inspect, update, delete, logs
  /tasks     list, inspect, logs
  /secrets   list, create, inspect, delete, update
  /configs   list, create, inspect, delete, update

Arguments for out: Podman - the engine this client is actually tested
against - does not implement Swarm at all, so half the matrix would be
untestable here. Compose and Kubernetes took the orchestration role Swarm
was aimed at. It is a lot of surface for something no current consumer asks
for.

Arguments for in: secrets and configs are useful on their own and are the
smallest two. Services would make the client able to deploy, not just build.

Wanted: a decision, and then either the work or a sentence in the POD saying
Swarm is out of scope, so the absence reads as a choice. Right now a reader
cannot tell "not yet" from "never".


--- DECISION 2026-08-27 (maintainer) ---
PARTIALLY IN. /secrets and /configs are implemented -- the two smallest, and
useful on their own. /swarm, /nodes, /services and /tasks stay OUT and get a
sentence in the POD saying so, so the absence reads as a choice rather than
as unfinished work.

2026-08-27 05:06 PARTIALLY IN, as decided. Implemented lib/API/Docker/API/Secrets.pm and
lib/API/Docker/API/Configs.pm with list/create/inspect/update/remove, removed
