Measured against Podman 5.4.2 / API 1.41, not extrapolated:
- Podman DOES serve /secrets, from its own local secret store, no swarm
  needed. The scaffold DESCRIPTION claimed the opposite and was corrected.
  create answers 200 (Docker documents 201); update answers 501 "update is
  not supported" with or without version.
- Podman does NOT serve /configs: 404 with a plain-text "Not Found" body.
- Data on the wire is base64 and the daemon does NOT validate it. Data set to
  the plain text "hello there!" was accepted with HTTP 200 and stored three
  bytes of garbage. That silent-corruption path is why this class encodes for
  the caller rather than expecting pre-encoded bytes.
- The alphabet is STANDARD base64, not URL-safe, despite the Engine API
  reference calling the field "base64-url-safe-encoded": +v/++w== stored
  correctly, the same bytes as -v_--w== were rejected 500.

update takes the version as a mandatory second positional argument and croaks
client-side when it is missing or non-numeric, naming inspect() and
Version.Index as the source.

